186430731 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430730 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430731 1069 "q-112213" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430731 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430731 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430731 1072 #uuid "7fd80750-80bf-5e1d-b08d-abec51a32d9d" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430731 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 40\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -10{x}_{2}=40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-4)=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430732 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430729 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430732 1069 "q-112202" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430732 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430732 1071 "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430732 1072 #uuid "8a5b5cd1-19ba-524a-960c-18e8a17d885d" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true] [17592186430732 1074 "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534643 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-2513b831-2bda-5222-a175-9dbc2cbe0fa3" 17592186430711 "answer-29376ce5-1709-5e3d-9b46-93794cef8b6b" 17592186430712 "answer-2ce43d07-7d46-5c98-b744-3a88ad395201" 17592186430713 "answer-54390e6e-dcb1-5dd3-95c7-15b36777dc0f" 17592186430714 "answer-5de78ea6-b293-58dc-961e-a74b7da29c90" 17592186430715 "answer-82bca19e-14cc-56cc-9397-e33111aae553" 17592186430716 "answer-8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" 17592186430717 "answer-8c8f1b4f-ea6f-50a7-90b7-28a18c762dfe" 17592186430718 "answer-916a198b-9533-5031-bb1d-8a1a6d13d6a1" 17592186430719 "answer-a1f552c7-b78f-5465-9564-878cf6243fe9" 1759218